From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d2d1: image brushes paint any image; command lists record BlendImage

An image brush painted only a whole bitmap ('Only image brushes with bitmaps are supported'): an effect's output, a command list, an image source or a source rectangle inside a bitmap drew nothing or the whole bitmap. Before each use, what is not a whole bitmap is now drawn with DrawImage on a device context of the same device into a bitmap of the source rectangle (the image's local bounds when the rectangle is empty), at the target's DPI, placed at the rectangle's position in brush space, with the brush's extend and interpolation modes. The bitmap and image brush matrix also scaled the transform's columns instead of the bitmap's axes, so a rotated non-square bitmap was mapped wrong (scale, then origin, then brush transform now). BlendImage into a command list target is recorded and blends when the list is drawn (ID2D1CommandSink5 is not declared, so other sinks are not given it); it was dropped. Wine's own image brush test with a 1 x 1 source rectangle now matches the Windows surface (its todo_wine is dropped).
